  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Drier and cooler weather will return for the end of \nthe work week. \n\nAn upper level trough will move across northern Ontario and Quebec \ntoday. A cold front will move across the region this morning. Behind\nthe front, west-southwest winds will veer to the northwest, and\ndrier air will filter into the region. An isolated shower along\nthe front early this morning cannot be ruled out. \n\nSurface high pressure over the Midwest will build toward the eastern \nGreat Lakes region today. A progressive shortwave trough is expected \nto meet with a frontal boundary south of the region this afternoon. \nAn isolated shower is possible across the western Southern Tier. The \nsurface high will settle across the region through the end of the \nwork week bringing cooler, dry weather. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Warmer weather combined with increasing humidity will \nsupport the chance of showers and thunderstorms beginning \nSaturday.\n\nA southerly flow will transport warm, moist air into the region \nSaturday. Diurnally-driven showers and thunderstorms are possible \nespecially across western NY. An upper level trough and cold front \nmay move across the region Sunday. Showers and thunderstorms are \npossible, however confidence is low on timing and strength at this \ntime.",
